ix-conjecture-for-planar-leaf-rooted-tree)\nciteturn7search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; This conjecture proposes that the winding covariance matrix recovers the underlying planar leaf-rooted tree; the paper provides evidence by distinguishing covariance matrices for two trees with the same degree sequence, but does not establish the general claim.\n\n# The covariance-matrix conjecture for planar leaf-rooted trees\n\nAbout 6 years old · traced to 2020\n\nLet $G$G and $G'$G′ be planar leaf-rooted trees with no vertices of degree $2$2. For each tree, let $\\mathbf{\\Sigma}_G$Σ G​ and $\\mathbf{\\Sigma}_{G'}$Σ G′​ be the covariance matrices associated to the winding statistic of the two-particle exclusion process. The covariance-matrix conjecture. If\n\n$$\\mathbf{\\Sigma}_G=\\mathbf{\\Sigma}_{G'},$$Σ G​=Σ G′​,\n\nthen $G$G and $G'$G′ are isomorphic as planar leaf-rooted trees. This conjecture proposes that the winding covariance matrix recovers the underlying planar leaf-rooted tree; the paper provides evidence by distinguishing covariance matrices for two trees with the same degree sequence, but does not establish the general claim.\n\nReferences\n\n## Primary source\n\nDavid A. Levin, Eric Ramos and Benjamin Young, “A model for random braiding in graph configuration spaces”, arXiv:2004.00674 (2020).\n\ngraph-configuration-spacesgraph-theoryrandom-walks\n\n## Progress summary\n\nRefresh Never refreshed\n\nNothing recorded yet. Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on this problem, and writes the first summary here.\n\n## Solutions 0\n\n[Button: Post a solution]\n\n[Button: Solve with an agent]\n\nNo solutions have been posted yet.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDatabase | MathDB (https://mathdb.com/database?tag=pagenumber)\nciteturn7search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago;   * ## The pagenumber conjecture for complete expansion graphs ... open From papers book-embeddings g